Z||000003||WKDFIRO||04-23-2001||09:40 PM||||Okay, 87 headlights are ridiculously easy to rebuild!!! I just did mine! Does eveyone have a problem with the Driver's side head light first? Seems to be a trend that I have seen through the years.<P>What usually happens is that the bushing inside the motor after a while become the same consistance as granulated sugar. The motor can't lift the hood door because it doesn't have anything inside of it to push on. It looks and sounds like a power problem but isn't.<P>I got replacement bushings from FOCOA (the dealer discontinued the bushing part number) for I think 6 bucks or something like that. Unbolt 3 bolts from the only circular plate you will see on the motor. Dump whats left of the other bushings and plop the 3 bushings in their place! Bolt it back up and you got headlights again!<P>Let us know how it goes!||||reg||6
